# Lesson 2, from the Lesson 2 bidding exercise 2e (partner opens 1C).
title: Partner opens 1♣: the jump raise
id: L02-25
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.3, 2.6
student: S
board: 25
dealer: N
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  KJ5    KJ6    Q72    QJ94
  E  T762   874    9853   A5
  S  A9     QT9    KJ4    KT732
  W  Q843   A532   AT6    86

auction:
  N 1C     = 13+ points, at least four clubs
  E Pass
  S 3C*    = an opening hand or better and four or more clubs: forcing to game
     key: 13 HCP and five clubs. With an opening hand and four-card support, raise to 3.
     not 2C: 2♣ shows 6-9. Did you count 13?
     not 2NT: 2NT is for hands without good support. Five clubs is good support.
     not 1D: You have five-card support. Isn't the raise the first thing to show?
     not *: With an opening hand or better and club support, which raise shows both?
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = Balanced: prefers game in no-trump
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: A club game needs about 28 points; 3NT needs only 25. Partner chose the easier game. Pass.
     not 4C: A club game needs 11 tricks and about 28 points. 3NT needs only 9. Which is easier?
     not 5C: A club game needs 11 tricks and about 28 points. 3NT needs only 9. Which is easier?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your 3♣ showed an opening hand or better and club support, enough for game. Partner,
  with a balanced hand, chose 3NT: nine tricks are easier than the eleven
  a club game needs. North is declarer, because he bid no-trump first, and
  so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E S2  S S9  W SQ  N SK
  2   N CQ  E C5  S C2  W C6
      note: Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A and then the ♥A, keeping the spade winners as stoppers.
  3   N CJ  E CA  S C3  W C8
      note: Keep leading clubs until the ace is gone.
  4   E ST  S SA  W S3  N S5
  5   S CK  W H2  N C4  E D3
      note: Now run the clubs.
  6   S CT  W H3  N C9  E H4
      note: Keep going.
  7   S C7  W H5  N D2  E D5
      note: The last club.
  8   S HQ  W HA  N H6  E H7
      note: Now drive out the ♥A.
  9   W S8  N SJ  E S6  S D4
  10  N HK  E H8  S H9  W D6
      note: The heart winners.
  11  N HJ  E S7  S HT  W DT
      note: And another.
  12  N DQ  E D8  S DJ  W DA
      note: Lead a diamond. West takes the ace.
  13  W S4  N D7  E D9  S DK
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: drive out the ♣A and the ♥A, keeping the spade winners
  as stoppers.

  3NT made. Your raise told partner about the fit and the strength, and he
  picked the game that needs fewer tricks.
